
  <main id="main">

    <section class="page-head industry-head page-head--art">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">For plumbers and trades</span>
        <h1>When the geyser bursts, be the one who answers.</h1>
        <figure class="ph-art ph-art--phone" aria-hidden="true"><img src="assets/art/phone-call.webp?v=2" alt="" width="600" height="1005" /></figure>
        <p class="lead">Missed calls, WhatsApps at 11pm and &ldquo;how much for a geyser?&rdquo;: followed up in seconds. Voicemails and WhatsApps turned into job cards, jobs offered a slot from your diary, and real emergencies sent straight to whoever is on call.</p>
        <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:1.4rem">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--large" href="https://calendar.app.google/58FYamh1ahXB4khM9" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="cta-plumbers-book">Book a free 30-minute call</a>
          <a href="live-demo?sample=calls" class="btn btn--ghost btn--large" data-track="cta-plumbers-demo">See it follow one up</a>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted" data-contact-block hidden>Rather message? <a class="inline-link" href="#" data-contact="whatsapp" hidden>WhatsApp us</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="painTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Where the day goes</span><h2 id="painTitle">The messages that eat your day.</h2></div>
        <div class="grid grid--3">
          <div class="card reveal"><span class="card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/><path d="m16 2 6 6M22 2l-6 6"/></svg></span><h3>Calls you can&rsquo;t take</h3><p>You&rsquo;re under a sink. The call goes to voicemail, and the customer calls the next plumber on Google.</p></div>
          <div class="card reveal"><span class="card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 12.8A9 9 0 1 1 11.2 3a7 7 0 0 0 9.8 9.8z"/></svg></span><h3>Quotes typed at night</h3><p>Every &ldquo;how much for&hellip;?&rdquo; needs a reply with your call-out and rates, written after a full day on site.</p></div>
          <div class="card reveal"><span class="card__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h16.9a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"/><path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"/></svg></span><h3>Emergencies mixed in with admin</h3><p>A burst pipe at 6am sits in the same inbox as a newsletter. The urgent ones need to reach you first.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="setTitle">
      <div class="container service__grid">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">What we&rsquo;d set up</span>
          <h2 id="setTitle">AI drafts the reply. You stay in charge.</h2>
          <ul class="tick-list">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg> <span>Missed callers pointed to WhatsApp by your voicemail greeting, and answered there straight away</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg> <span>Voicemails written up as job cards, where your phone line can send them by email</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg> <span>Routine jobs offered a slot from your diary</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg> <span>Emergencies sent to the on-call person straight away</span></li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg> <span>Quote replies drafted from your call-out fee and rates</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:1rem">It answers only from your own prices and rules. Anything it isn&rsquo;t sure about goes to a person.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="industry-demos">
          <a class="card card--link work-card reveal" href="live-demo?sample=calls">
            <div class="work-card__body">
              <div class="work-card__meta"><span class="badge badge--concept">Live demo</span><span class="tag tag--muted">Sample work, nothing is sent</span></div>
              <h3>A missed call, followed up</h3>
              <p>A caller&rsquo;s geyser isn&rsquo;t heating. The voicemail becomes a job card, and a WhatsApp with a slot and the call-out price is ready to send.</p>
              <div class="card__foot"><span class="card__more">Run it yourself</span></div>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="pricing" aria-labelledby="priceTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal"><span class="eyebrow">What it costs</span><h2 id="priceTitle">A fixed price before anything starts.</h2></div>
        <div class="grid grid--2 industry-pricing">
          <div class="reveal">
            <ul class="price-list">
            <li><div class="pl-name">WhatsApp and enquiry assistant<small>Replies drafted from your prices and diary, on WhatsApp and your website. Then from <span data-zar="7500">R7,500</span>/mo to keep it running (3-month minimum, then month to month)</small></div><span class="price"><small>from</small><span data-zar="25000">R25,000</span></span></li>
            <li><div class="pl-name">Lots of customer email (20+ a day)? Inbox Assistant<small>Routine email replies drafted for your team. <span data-zar="9500">R9,500</span> setup + <span data-zar="2950">R2,950</span>/mo, with a <span data-zar="1500">R1,500</span> deposit to start, refunded in full if it doesn&rsquo;t save 5 hours a week</small></div><span class="price"><small>setup</small><span data-zar="9500">R9,500</span></span></li>
            <li><div class="pl-name">Add a website<small>A fast site with tap-to-call and a quote tool</small></div><span class="price"><small>from</small><span data-zar="12500">R12,500</span></span></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:.8rem">40% deposit, the rest at go-live. It drafts replies to your real messages before it goes live, and you can stop after any stage.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="industry-side">
          <div class="card card--tint reveal">
            <h3>Not sure it&rsquo;s worth it?</h3>
            <p>That&rsquo;s what the free call is for. Tell us roughly how many messages and calls you get. We&rsquo;ll tell you honestly whether AI would save real hours, and if not, we&rsquo;ll say so.</p>
            <p style="margin-top:.6rem">Only a few messages a day? We&rsquo;ll say so on the call. WhatsApp Business quick replies and an away message may be all you need, and they&rsquo;re free.</p>
            <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:0.8rem">Prices are starting points for typical plumbers. Your quote is fixed before we begin. <a class="inline-link" href="pricing">Full price list &rarr;</a></p>
          </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="howTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal"><span class="eyebrow">How it works</span><h2 id="howTitle">From first call to answered messages.</h2></div>
        <ol class="steps steps--4 reveal">
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">1</span><h3>Free 30-minute call</h3><p>You tell us what comes in and what eats your day. We say honestly whether AI fits.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">2</span><h3>Fixed quote</h3><p>Exactly what it will do and what it costs. Nothing starts until you&rsquo;ve said yes.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">3</span><h3>Tested on real messages</h3><p>It drafts replies to your real enquiries first, so you see it working before it goes live.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">4</span><h3>Running, and measured</h3><p>We look after it and send you the time it saved each month.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faqTitle">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section__head reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Questions plumbers ask</span><h2 id="faqTitle">Straight answers.</h2></div>
        <div class="faq reveal">
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Does it talk to callers on the phone?</summary><p>No. It doesn&rsquo;t answer calls. You keep your number: your voicemail greeting and WhatsApp away message point callers to WhatsApp, where the assistant answers straight away. If your phone line can send voicemails by email, those become job cards too.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Does it reply by itself?</summary><p>Only where you choose. We start with drafts and job cards for the office to send. Routine bookings can go out by themselves later, if you switch that on.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What about real emergencies?</summary><p>Anything urgent, a burst pipe, a gas smell, no power, goes to the on-call person immediately, not into a queue.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What if it stops working at night?</summary><p>Your calls and WhatsApps still come straight to you, exactly as they do today, so nothing is lost. We fix it the next business morning, as part of the monthly plan.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Who will we deal with?</summary><p>A small studio: the person on your free call builds it and answers your messages, with no call centre or hand-offs. It&rsquo;s documented and runs in accounts you own, so any developer can pick it up.</p></details>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:1.2rem">More in the <a class="inline-link" href="pricing#faq">general FAQ</a>. Also for: <a class="inline-link" href="for-accountants">Accounting & professional firms</a> · <a class="inline-link" href="for-salons">Salons</a> · <a class="inline-link" href="for-restaurants">Restaurants</a> · <a class="inline-link" href="for-cleaners">Cleaning services</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta" aria-labelledby="ctaTitle">
      <div class="container cta__inner reveal">
        <span class="cta__services">For plumbers and trades</span>
        <h2 id="ctaTitle">Tell us what takes too long.</h2>
        <p>A free 30-minute call on Google Meet, or we phone you. You leave with a rough price, or an honest &ldquo;not worth it&rdquo;.</p>
        <div class="btn-row btn-row--center">
          <a class="btn btn--light btn--large" href="https://calendar.app.google/58FYamh1ahXB4khM9" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="cta-plumbers-book-end">Book a free 30-minute call</a>
        </div>
        <p class="cta__alt">Rather we phone you? <button type="button" class="inline-link" data-call-open>Pick a time</button> &middot; Prefer to write? <button type="button" class="inline-link" data-review-open>Tell us in two lines</button></p>
        <p class="small muted" data-contact-block hidden>Rather message? <a class="inline-link" href="#" data-contact="whatsapp" hidden>WhatsApp us</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
